fftw3-hpx (2026-10-22)
=====================

The hpx/ directory ports FFTW 3.3.11's distributed-memory library to HPX
localities, collectives and channels, retaining the original algorithms and
planner hooks. FFTW's existing thread callback runs worker jobs on HPX
large-stack threads. Configure with --enable-hpx --enable-threads and the HPX
pkg-config path; double, single and long-double precision are supported.
See hpx/README.md for the SPMD application contract and build/test commands,
and hpx/VALIDATION.md for source provenance, exact checks and local results.

This repository starts from the official release tarball, including its
already-generated codelets:
  https://fftw.org/fftw-3.3.11.tar.gz
SHA256:
  5630c24cdeb33b131612f7eb4b1a9934234754f9f388ff8617458d0be6f239a1
Do not use the upstream Git bootstrap instructions below for this port;
its release sources build with autotools without OCaml or maintainer mode.

TCP is permitted only between localities on the same server. Cross-server
runs must use HPX's MPI parcelport with TCP disabled. The supplied local
check targets launch processes on one server only.

